|~ What is declared under `::each`, the step `*` runs on each
   element: its refusals. ~|

:each/construct
  |~~ The step `* body` from the quote of its body. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:each/PayloadNotQuoteError
  |~~ The payload of `::each` is the quote of its body.
      ::link~(::each | doc)
  ~~|

:each/PayloadNotQuoteError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(42 | tag ::each !| [type /actualType] | eq [::each/PayloadNotQuoteError ::number])

:each/ReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The `::each` prints as text that reads back as another step, or
      as none: a body holds at least one step.
      ::link~(::each | doc)
  ~~|

:each/ReadBackDiffersError/refusesAnEmptyBody
  |~~ An each of an empty body prints as text that reads back as none. ~~|
  ::law~(~() | tag ::each !| [type /printed] | eq [::each/ReadBackDiffersError "* ()"])

:each/ReadBackDiffersError/printed
  |~~ The text the step prints as, which reads back as another step or as none. ~~|
  ::string

:each/SubjectNotContainerError
  |~~ `*` runs its step on each element of a vector or a set, or on each
      value of a map; a value of another kind has no elements, and `|`
      runs a step on it whole.
      ::link~(::each | doc)
  ~~|

:each/SubjectNotContainerError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number has no elements to run on. ~~|
  ::law~(42 * add 1 !| [type /actualType] | eq [::each/SubjectNotContainerError ::number])
